  "prompt": "# The Feed — package prompt\n\nThis is the living spec for each weekly package. It is editable from the app\n(Settings → Package prompt) and synced back here. Each new package is\ngenerated from this file, `tools/data/config.json`, and the newest file in\n`feedback/`.\n\n## Goals\n- Replace 3–5 hours/day of doomscrolling with a feed that is curious, weird and kind.\n- One package lasts a full week (target: 5 h/day × 7 days) with **no repeated posts**,\n  and nothing repeated from earlier packages.\n- Mostly offline. Only videos (and, optionally, images) need the network.\n- Keep AI-generated images and text to a minimum unless a category asks for it.\n- Use favorites, saves and more/less marks from `feedback/` to steer the next package.\n\n## Categories and share of the feed\n\n### Physics games — 20%\nSimple 2D physics games: bouncing objects, merging items, breaking blocks,\nside-scrolling dash mechanics and other classic casual styles. Each card runs on\nauto-pilot when it appears and becomes playable when tapped.\n\n### Condensed Wikipedia — 30%\nArticles condensed to 5 sentences or fewer. Each card shows a one-sentence hook;\ntapping it expands the summary and links to the full article. Topics:\n- **Music history**: all genres, especially underground trip-hop, punk, avant-garde,\n  electronic, hip-hop, heavy metal and transgressive experimental.\n- **Literature**: all genres, especially sci-fi, sex and erotica, Beat Generation authors,\n  esoteric and occult, experimental, offbeat non-fiction, poetry and alternative science.\n- **Science**: especially biology, sociology, psychology, technology and mathematics.\n- **History**: especially revolutionary periods, indigenous history and art history.\n- **Transgressive art**: especially queer artists and artists imprisoned or persecuted for their work.\n- **Unsolved mysteries**: especially esoteric and supernatural mysteries.\n- **Occult and religious customs**: indigenous spirituality, Gnosticism and cult activities.\n\n### YouTube videos — 20%\nMostly short videos and reels. They autoplay muted and have an unmute button. Topics:\ncute animals, retro gaming, vintage sci-fi and fantasy films and shows, plus every\nWikipedia topic above.\n\n### Memes — 10%\nHumorous images juxtaposed with snippets from the Wikipedia section, plus quotes\nfrom Robert Anton Wilson, William S. Burroughs, Tom Robbins and other offbeat authors.\nAlso memes collected from knowyourmeme.com.\n\n### Made-up products — 5%\nWeird, absurd products that don't exist and serve surreal purposes, with 80s/90s-style\npromo graphics and absurdist product descriptions.\n\n### Psychedelic visuals — 5%\nFractals, tunnels, fading colors and other generative, math-based imagery, each with a\nshort quote from the sections above.\n\n### Self-care reminders — 5%\nPrompts to make art and music, go for walks, work out, breathe, meditate and so on.\n\n### From around the web — 5%\nCarefully picked posts and articles from Substack, Hacker News and occasionally Reddit,\nchosen to match the topics above.\n",
